  "notes": "Impedance (EIS) sweeps 0.1 Hz-5 kHz are interleaved with charge and discharge cycles. Cathode/format come from the registry; the README says only 'Li-ion'. Stated end of life: 30% fade of the rated capacity (2 to 1.4 Ah). Charging profile: the charge step is the same CC-CV in every set; the C-rate differs between cells through the discharge current. The registry ref_name says 1C_1C_25T, which fits only some cells (2 A discharge, 25 degC); the README lists 1, 2 and 4 A discharges and 4 to 44 degC. Primary source: not a paper but the dataset citation B. Saha and K. Goebel (2007), 'Battery Data Set', NASA Prognostics Data Repository, NASA Ames Research Center (PCoE Data Set Repository entry 5; also DASHlink resource 133, issued 2010-09-13, whose plain-text source and documentation links on ti.arc.nasa.gov no longer resolve). It describes 18650 cells rated 2 Ah run to 30% fade (1.4 Ah) with charge, discharge and EIS tests at different temperatures and discharge cut-offs below the OEM 2.7 V."
